            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nThis appeared to be an upstream Neovim issue: neovim/neovim#31680. It manifested itself because `vim.ui.select()` from 'mini.pick' executes its callback with floating window being current *and* `MiniSessions.read()` executes `:%bwipeout!` to have clean session loading.\r\n\r\nAs this is indeed not really a common case to do (specifically executing \"read session\" in combination with \"execute in new tabpage\"), I am going to close this as \"not the issue with 'mini.nvim' and more of upstream Neovim issue\".",
